  <ai_direction_summary>The AI used a single mod-3 coloring to get 9 candidate missing cells, then applied a D4 symmetry argument to eliminate 8 of them (showing each non-center candidate maps under rotation to a non-color-1 cell which cannot be missing), leaving only the center, then performed an exhaustive 4x4 binary matrix enumeration to count tilings.</ai_direction_summary>
  <standard_solution_key_technique>The standard solution uses two simultaneous mod-3 colorings of the board so that the intersection of "must-be-uncovered" cells from both colorings uniquely identifies the center, then forces the tiling by a simple WLOG placement argument.</standard_solution_key_technique>
